-/* ── FluentCard popup / dropdown clipping fix ─────────────────────────
-   This component hosts FluentSelect and CodedValueDropdown controls
-   inside several FluentCard panels. The <fluent-card> host style is
-   `:host{ display:block; contain:content }`. `contain:paint` clips
-   descendants to the card's padding box independent of `overflow`, and
-   `contain:layout` makes the card a containing block for `position:fixed`
-   descendants. That clips the popup lists used by the dropdowns.
-
-   Fixing the card alone is not enough because the layout's `.page-scroll`
-   (`MainLayout.razor.css`, overflow:auto) is the sole scroll region and
-   also clips a `position:absolute` popup that extends past its bottom
-   edge. The pragmatic fix is:
-     1. `contain: none !important` on the card — removes paint clipping and
-        removes the card as a fixed containing block.
-     2. `position: fixed !important` on the popup elements — the anchored
-        region inside FluentSelect / CodedValueDropdown uses delta-based
-        viewport positioning, so fixed placement still positions correctly
-        under the trigger, and it escapes .page-scroll overflow.
-
-   Reference: microsoft/fluentui-blazor#2791 (closed with only a CSS
-   workaround; no library fix as of FluentUI v4.14.2).
-
-   The same workaround is used in GuardianDetail.razor.css,
-   GuardiansTab.razor.css, and GradeLevelWizard.razor.css; keep them in
-   sync. */
-.detail-card {
-    overflow: visible;
-    contain: none !important;
-}
-
-::deep .detail-card .fluent-popup-body,
-::deep .detail-card .fluent-listbox {
-    position: fixed !important;
-}
